## Dystopia: real diseases, their symptoms and medicines (entity names come from the prototypes)

# --- Symptom popups ---
disease-effect-popup-blood-cough = You cough violently, there is blood on your lips.
disease-effect-popup-breathless = You are short of breath.
disease-effect-popup-rash = An itchy red rash covers your skin.
disease-effect-popup-itch = Your skin itches unbearably.
disease-effect-popup-ring-rash = Scaly rings on your skin itch.
disease-effect-popup-dehydration = Your stomach cramps and you feel very thirsty.
disease-effect-popup-wasting = Your stomach rumbles no matter how much you eat.
disease-effect-popup-jaundice = Your skin and eyes have turned yellow. Your right side aches.
disease-effect-popup-buboes = Painful lumps swell in your armpits and groin.
disease-effect-popup-hydrophobia = The very thought of water makes your throat seize.
disease-effect-popup-rage = You are overwhelmed by senseless rage!
disease-effect-popup-ataxia = Your legs don't obey you.

# --- Medicines ---
reagent-name-oseltamivir = oseltamivir
reagent-desc-oseltamivir = A mild antiviral with no side effects. Good against flu and other viruses.
reagent-name-ribavirin = ribavirin
reagent-desc-ribavirin = A strong broad-spectrum antiviral. Destroys red blood cells, causing blood loss.
reagent-name-amoxicillin = amoxicillin
reagent-desc-amoxicillin = A broad-spectrum antibiotic against bacterial infections. No side effects at a normal dose.
reagent-name-doxycycline = doxycycline
reagent-desc-doxycycline = An antibiotic. Also works weakly against parasites. Good against plague and cholera.
reagent-name-isoniazid = isoniazid
reagent-desc-isoniazid = The strongest anti-tuberculosis antibiotic. Toxic to the liver.
reagent-name-albendazole = albendazole
reagent-desc-albendazole = An anthelmintic. Kills tapeworms and other parasites.
reagent-name-ivermectin = ivermectin
reagent-desc-ivermectin = An antiparasitic, especially against mites (scabies). Overdose causes seizures and poisoning.
reagent-name-fluconazole = fluconazole
reagent-desc-fluconazole = An antifungal with no serious side effects.
reagent-name-amphotericin-b = amphotericin B
reagent-desc-amphotericin-b = A very strong antifungal for severe cases. Toxic to the kidneys.
reagent-name-pentosan-polysulfate = pentosan polysulfate
reagent-desc-pentosan-polysulfate = An experimental anti-prion drug. Slowly halts and reverses prion disease. Thins the blood.

